Title: The Last Ferry
Credit: an example screenplay for script2comic
Author: Mano Samy
Draft date: November 2026

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - NIGHT

A cramped office above the pier. Rain on the window. A wall clock reads 11:52.

MIRA (30s, the harbor master's deputy, sleeves rolled) stamps a ledger shut and reaches for the light switch.

The door bangs open. KOFI (50s, ferry captain, soaked oilskins) fills the frame.

KOFI
Don't turn that off.

MIRA
Last boat left at eleven. You were on it.

KOFI
(beat)
I turned her around.

He drops a child's red mitten on the desk. It is still wet.

MIRA
(quiet)
Where did you find that?

KOFI
Floating. Two hundred yards off the point.

A phone on the wall starts to ring. Neither of them moves.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
(filtered)
Harbor office, this is Pier Nine. We have a boy here asking for his mother.

Mira looks at the mitten. Then at the clock. 11:53.

EXT. PIER NINE - NIGHT

Rain in the floodlights. A small boy, TEO (6), sits on a bollard wrapped in a blanket far too big for him. He holds one red mitten.

[[skip]] Mira runs the length of the pier. Kofi follows, slower.

TEO
Did you find the other one?

MIRA
(kneeling)
We did.

She presses the wet mitten into his hand. He puts both on, solemnly, and holds them up to the light.

TEO
Now we can go.

Kofi laughs, once, like something breaking loose.

KOFI
Last ferry. All aboard.

FADE OUT.
